{
  "area": "saves-tutorial-progress",
  "description": "NEGATIVE CONTROL for tutorial_progress_corpus_negative (PL.native-tutorial-save): core's tutorial progress corpus with a wrong contract table, a wrong runner list, four wrong answers and one case no row can drive. The runner must FAIL it, naming each. Inputs are synthetic and copied from the vendored corpus (corebridge/vendor/core/conformance/saves/tutorial-progress.json); never a source of truth.",
  "version": 1,
  "sources": [
    "New in core (PL.tutorial-progress-save): the Unreal P8 landing (run 7, p8-unreal) found tutorial progress missing from core's save. Inputs are synthetic; every expected is core's answer.",
    "The lessons, events and bindings are conformance/quests/tutorial.json's (P8.core); its cases are unchanged."
  ],
  "tolerance": 1e-9,
  "contract": {
    "ops": [
      "tutorial",
      "onboarding"
    ],
    "tutorialSteps": [
      "start",
      "event",
      "complete",
      "skip",
      "skipNonAssessment",
      "tick"
    ],
    "onboardingSteps": [
      "start",
      "complete",
      "skip",
      "event",
      "tick",
      "save"
    ],
    "clockStart": "2026-11-06T09:00:00.000Z",
    "extensionKey": "tutorial",
    "blockMembers": [
      "completed",
      "skipped",
      "current"
    ],
    "saveRule": "saveProgress() = {completed: the objectives the player completed, skipped: the objectives a skip passed (each in the tutorial's order, then any a restored save named that this tutorial does not run, in the save's order), current: the current objective, null once the tutorial is over, endedBySkip: a skip ended it}. The manager's, before start: the progress it was given (a copy), or null when it was given none (the save carries the stored block untouched).",
    "loadRule": "progress restores without raising anything: completed objectives are done, skipped ones done by a skip, and the first objective left in the tutorial's order is current; start() announces it, and the clock (startedAt, durations) counts from that start. current null restores a tutorial that is over (endedBySkip as saved), passing as skipped any objective the save does not name. Ids the tutorial does not run are kept for saveProgress().",
    "freshRule": "no block (stored absent: a new game's save or one written before the block; or null, the registry default after migrateExtensions) is no progress: the tutorial starts fresh, its first lesson current.",
    "readRule": "readable: an object; completed and skipped absent ([]) or lists of non-empty ids, no repeat, no id in both; current required, null or a non-empty id in neither list; endedBySkip absent (false) or a boolean, true only when current is null and skipped names an objective. Otherwise {read: {ok: false, keys}}, keys = the unreadable members (completed, completed[<i>], skipped, skipped[<i>], current, endedBySkip) in ascending string order (empty when the block is not an object), and no tutorial is built."
  },
